# GEA3-U2 — 290 typed F32 full-model tensor views, manifest-bound.
#
# This is the model-to-kernel admission seam for the whole frozen model,
# the GEA2-U2 nine-tensor pattern (gradus:model/block_view) widened to the
# full census: 32 layers × 9 block tensors + token_embd.weight +
# output_norm.weight + the tied lm_head → token_embd.weight row. The
# source adapter reads one bounded absolute range and supplies its identity
# claims; this module retains only typed resident bytes and manifest facts.
# It has no path, reader, container, GGUF parser, or physical-device input.
#
# Every expected shape, range, and tensor digest below is copied from the
# frozen U1 manifest:
# radix/docs/factory/gpu-execution-architecture/evidence/gea3-input-manifest.json
# (header-derived; 290 tensors, 361,821,120 F32 values, 1,447,284,480 bytes).
# Logical shapes are the [out,in] boundary shapes; the GGUF header order is
# [in,out]. The per-layer absolute starts are copied verbatim: the GGUF file
# stores the 32 layers in lexicographic blk-name order (0, 1, 10..19, 2,
# 20..29, 3, 30, 31, 4..9), not in numeric order — ranges are never derived
# arithmetically here.

import from "gradus:dtype" dtype

